  "description": "DUWMAM crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C80 H120 Mn2 N4 O58 Tb6,C2 H3 N1,24(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Tb1B (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb2B (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb3B (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Mn1B (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Tb4? (Tb) has 0 O neighbors; Tb5? (Tb) has 0 O neighbors; Tb6? (Tb) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 8 pairs, 5 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.373-4.021 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.08-112.44°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C80H120Mn2N4O58Tb6·C2H3N·24(H2O). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
